# Usercentrics

> Usercentrics provides consent infrastructure for 2.4 million websites and apps across 195 countries, processing 8.8 billion consents monthly. The company operates two brands: Usercentrics (mid-market and enterprise) and Cookiebot by Usercentrics (SMB and mid-market). Products span web, mobile, and connected TV consent management, server-side tracking, AI data governance, privacy policy generation, and preference management. Usercentrics GmbH is headquartered in Munich, Germany; Cookiebot is operated by Usercentrics A/S, registered in Denmark.

Usercentrics is not a legal services provider, data broker, analytics platform, or general-purpose privacy consultancy. Compliance with applicable laws remains the responsibility of the website or app operator.

## Products

### Privacy Compliance

- [Web CMP](https://usercentrics.com/website-consent-management/): Consent management platform for websites. Automates consent collection, auto-blocks non-essential services, and provides customizable banners. Available in two tiers: Cookiebot Core CMP (plug-and-play for SMBs) and Usercentrics Advanced CMP (enterprise-grade, with advanced analytics and A/B testing).
- [App CMP](https://usercentrics.com/in-app-sdk/): Mobile SDK for iOS and Android. Supports GDPR, CCPA, TCF v2.2, and other frameworks. Includes A/B testing and analytics.
- [CTV CMP](https://usercentrics.com/usercentrics-ctv-cmp/): Consent management for connected TV and OTT streaming apps. Supports cross-device consent sharing.
- [Privacy Policy Generator](https://usercentrics.com/privacy-policy-generator/): Generates privacy policies supporting GDPR, US state laws, and multiple languages. Provides automated updates for legal and technical changes.

### Server-Side Tracking

- [Server-Side Tagging (sGTM)](https://usercentrics.com/server-side-tracking-solution/): Server-side Google Tag Manager solution. Centralizes first-party data for Google, Meta, TikTok, and other destinations. Improves data quality, page performance, and marketing attribution.
- [Meta Signals Gateway](https://usercentrics.com/meta-signals-gateway/): Sends high-quality web and offline conversion signals to Meta. Supports Pixel and Conversions API (CAPI) integrations, custom audience building, and offline conversion imports.

### AI Data Governance

- [MCP Manager](https://usercentrics.com/ai-model-context-protocol-manager/): Governance layer for AI systems using the Model Context Protocol (MCP). Enables businesses to control, monitor, and audit AI access to business and consumer data. Features include audit logs, PII access controls, and token usage management.

### Consent and Preference

- [Preference Manager](https://usercentrics.com/preference-management/): Preference Management Platform (PMP) for zero- and first-party data. Centralizes visitor consent and preferences and passes them to advertising platforms and marketing stacks.
- [Audience Unlocker](https://usercentrics.com/audience-unlocker/) *(Early Access)*: Retargeting tool built on consented first-party data.

